LEGION & IDEAPAD EC FAN CONTROL Documentation for Gen 5/6/7/8/9/10

----------------------------------------------------

GEN 5-7 (excludes the 2020 L7, 2020 IG3, 2020 L7 Slim, 2021 IG3, and 2022 L7, 2022 L7 Slim.)

----------------------------------------------------

Technical Info:

-------------------------------------

C530: Mode indicator, read only.
C531: Indicates the fan curve is in the low temperature mode or not (changes overwritten instantly, low temp curve: 1 normal curve: 2)
C534: Indicates the fan curve level the fans are currently at.
C535: Indicates the fan curve endpoint, can be changed to increase the fan curve length(the fans will ignore values that are placed after the endpoint)
C538: CPU Temperature
C539: GPU Temperature (can be disabled by setting C4BD to 20)
C53A: PCH Temperature
C5FC: CPU Fan Target RPM
C5FD: GPU Fan Target RPM
C4AB: Disable EC fan control by setting to 8, enable by 0.

-------------------------------------

FAN CONTROL

-------------------------------------

C5E0&E1: CPU Fan TACH High and Low bits, read it in 16bit and you get the full fan RPM
C5E2&E3: GPU Fan TACH High and Low bits, read it in 16bit and you get the full fan RPM

C5E4: CPU Fan Instant Set Register(will get overwritten by the fan curve once the fan speed change delay ends) (fan delay bypassable by setting this register and the fan curve at the same time)
C5E5: CPU Fan Instant Set Register(will get overwritten by the fan curve once the fan speed change delay ends) (fan delay bypassable by setting this register and the fan curve at the same time)

C5FE: is the CPU fan delay counter, counts up to 100 in 5 seconds, you can bypass the fan delay if you set it to 64.
C5FF: is the GPU fan delay counter, counts up to 100 in 5 seconds, you can bypass the fan delay if you set it to 64.

----------------------------------------------------

Fan Acceleration/Deceleration fix for 2020 models: 

C3DC: Fan 1 Acceleration
C3DD: Fan 2 Acceleration

C3DE: Fan 1 Deceleration
C3DF: Fan 2 Deceleration

----------------------------------------------------

FAN CURVE: 

----------------------------------------------------

C535: Indicates the amount of steps of the fan curve, can be changed to increase the fan curve length
(the fans will ignore values that are placed after the endpoint, and EC will crash if you set above 12 steps)

Max Fan Curve Step Count: 12 Steps

For CPU Fan, C541 to whatever value you set at C535
For GPU Fan, C551 to whatever value you set at C535

Fan Acceleration for both fan: C561 to whatever value you set at C535 (you can set different values for each steps in the curve)(doesn't work on 2020 models due to broken lenovo implementation)
Fan Deceleration for both fan: C571 to whatever value you set at C535 (you can set different values for each steps in the curve)(doesn't work on 2020 models due to broken lenovo implementation)

CPU Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: C581 to whatever value you set at C535
CPU Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: C591 to whatever value you set at C535 

GPU Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: C5A1 to whatever value you set at C535
GPU Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: C5B1 to whatever value you set at C535

PCH Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: C5C1 to whatever value you set at C535
PCH Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: C5D1 to whatever value you set at C535

Set 7F(127) to ignore values in the table.

----------------------------------------------------

GEN 8-10 (excludes LOQs except the 1st gen LOQ)

----------------------------------------------------

FAN CONTROL

----------------------------------------------------

DFD0&D1: CPU Fan TACH High and Low bits, read it in 16bit and you get the full fan RPM
DFD2&D3: GPU Fan TACH High and Low bits, read it in 16bit and you get the full fan RPM
DFD3&D4: SYS Fan TACH High and Low bits, read it in 16bit and you get the full fan RPM

---------------
2 Fan Legions:
---------------

DFDA: CPU Fan 1000ms Delay before changing speed
DFDA: GPU Fan 1000ms Delay before changing speed

DFE4: CPU Requested Fan Step
DFE5: GPU Requested Fan Step
DFE6: PCH Requested Fan Step
DFEA: Final Global Fan Step

DFD4: CPU Fan Apply RPM (*100)
DFD5: GPU Fan Apply RPM (*100)

DFD8: CPU Fan Target RPM (*100)
DFD9: GPU Fan Target RPM (*100)

DFF8: CPU Fan Current RPM (*100)
DFF9: GPU Fan Current RPM (*100)

DFE1: GPU Fan Target PWM
DFE2: CPU Fan Target PWM

---------------
3 Fan Legions:
---------------

DFD9: CPU Requested Fan Step
DFDA: GPU Requested Fan Step
DFDB: PCH Requested Fan Step
DFDE: Final Global Fan Step

DFE0: CPU Fan Target RPM (*100)
DFE1: GPU Fan Target RPM (*100)
DFE2: SYS Fan Target RPM (*100)

DFEC: CPU Fan Current RPM (*100)
DFED: GPU Fan Current RPM (*100)
DFEE: SYS Fan Current RPM (*100)

DFE8: GPU Fan Target PWM
DFE9: CPU Fan Target PWM
DFEA: SYS Fan Target PWM

----------------------------------------------------

FAN CURVE (Vertical offsets):

----------------------------------------------------

Max Fan Curve Step Count: 12 Steps

For CPU Fan, DF10 to DFB0
For GPU Fan, DF11 to DFB1
For SYS Fan, DF12 to DFB2

Fan Acceleration for both fan: DF04 to DFB4 (you can set different values for each steps in the curve)
Fan Deceleration for both fan: DF05 to DFB5 (you can set different values for each steps in the curve)

CPU Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: DF06 to DFB6
CPU Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: DF07 to DFB7

GPU Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: DF08 to DFB8
GPU Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: DF09 to DFB9

PCH Temp Thresholds for Ramp Up: DF0A to DFBA
PCH Temp Thresholds for Slow Down: DF0B to DFBB

Set 7F(127) to ignore values in the table.

